# Crit CLI operations

The active review path is shown by `crit status`. Prefer Crit's finish output when available; otherwise use:

```bash
crit comments            # unresolved comments
crit comments --json     # structured comments
crit comments --all      # include resolved comments
crit comments --plan <slug>
```

Add review, file, or line comments with `crit comment`. Always attribute comments to `OMP` and quote shell arguments safely:

```bash
crit comment --author 'OMP' 'Overall review comment'
crit comment --author 'OMP' src/auth.go:42 'Missing null check'
crit comment --reply-to <id> --author 'OMP' 'Addressed this'
```

Do not pass `--resolve` unless the user explicitly asks. Use `--plan <slug>` for plan review files. For three or more comments, use `crit comment --json --author 'OMP'` with the documented JSON schema; use a file for multiline bodies rather than hand-built shell quoting.

GitHub/GitLab synchronization:

```bash
crit pull [change-number-or-url]
crit push --dry-run [change-number]
crit push [--event comment|approve|request-changes] [change-number]
```

Sharing and cleanup:

```bash
crit share <file> [file...]
crit unpublish [file...]
```

Only share, publish, push, or unpublish when the user requests it. Relay Crit's full share output. Resolve comments only on explicit instruction.
